        "title": "Logitech announces two new keyboard cases for iPad",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/07/logitech-announces-two-new-keyboard-cases-for-ipad/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/05/Rugged_Combo_4c_Touch_and_Zone_Learn_LIFE_Orange_Blue_Listening-2-2.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p>Logitech today iPad (10th generation): the Rugged Combo 4c and Rugged Combo 4c Touch.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>In a press release, Logitech touts that these new cases offer a “fully sealed keyboard and a versatile USB-C port that enables students to charge iPad and use a wired headset at the same time.”</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"ipad\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1051383\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/07/logitech-announces-two-new-keyboard-cases-for-ipad/#more-1051383\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
